e9484392f","text":"It decreases","isCorrect":true,"position":3}]},{"id":"3f3a8d5f-b1d1-5868-a7d6-b8e894be337b","position":130,"prompt":"Why do nonpolar I₂ molecules attract one another?","explanation":"Large polarizable electron clouds produce significant London dispersion attractions.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","fingerprint":"1aad46b652cb1c900b847b1f09c47b3db2e55744f2ce87f1fceecd8e433b2730","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"Period 6; CHM 101 Chemical Bonding slides; Chapter 7","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_chm101_240_v1","sourceReference":"Period 6; CHM 101 Chemical Bonding slides; Chapter 7","calculationAndConceptCheckCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"6f897e09-e9dd-52d2-8ab5-d384ceae8362","text":"They share protons between molecules","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"cc7f4ea1-0e95-5f78-94a2-b2fd4d6432c9","text":"They form metallic bonds","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"12b730be-82ef-53a6-b001-de3dc7a85724","text":"Their electron clouds form instantaneous and induced dipoles","isCorrect":true,"position":2},{"id":"c7fb7eac-0bb5-53d7-b8ff-09f5c51307ce","text":"Each iodine is permanently ionic","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"1241b358-a1f7-56dc-811b-7e627a29149e","position":131,"prompt":"Which liquid should have greater viscosity if molecular sizes are comparable?","explanation":"Stronger attractions hinder molecular motion and flow.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","fingerprint":"ac1ad175c95dbcbec91b03b64546409d0fe89ab11649ea2c6dd304b4001f8e93","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"Period 6; CHM 101 Chemical Bonding slides; Chapter 7","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_chm101_240_v1","sourceReferen