 lone pairs but the molecule has no H directly bonded to O, N or F.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","fingerprint":"4584260212dbcf91057f4aeff65a1225ba8bab970a75241417df4c19ba77703a","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General CHM 101 enrichment: Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","sourceKind":"general_chm101","reviewedFromLocalFiles":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_chm101_240_v1","sourceReference":"General CHM 101 enrichment: Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","calculationAndConceptCheckCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"7ab0936a-c559-50a3-ac8b-d16c99cdace6","text":"CH₃OCH₃","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"7af37dac-f649-570c-b076-20bc4e23b01f","text":"CH₃OH","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"a08e5693-7e7a-5130-9684-bf33ddd552c4","text":"NH₃","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"bc78ee40-2ade-55c8-a476-4dfb792799ab","text":"HF","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"defaf635-3e21-597a-8c59-3f193d43ee35","position":137,"prompt":"Why is ethanol soluble in water?","explanation":"The polar O–H group interacts favourably with water through hydrogen bonding.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","fingerprint":"c08859c0c688b92606449c77398a56416e099b833d3c4d15c5df481dd1da01d9","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General CHM 101 enrichment: Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","sourceKind":"general_chm101","reviewedFromLocalFiles":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_chm101_240_v1","sourceReference":"General CHM 101 enrichment: Intermolecular Forces and Physical Properties","calculationAndConceptCheckCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"bf11602f-5a59-5370-8183-962aa4c61033","text":"It forms a metallic lattice","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"62c9ba65-fb58-5c9f-a225-c76b